  intro="Chitré is Panama's cultural capital — home to the country's most famous Carnival, colonial-era traditions dating to 1558, and the most modern public hospital on the Azuero Peninsula. For expats who want a real Panamanian city experience at a fraction of the costs in more-marketed destinations, Chitré delivers. The expat community is smaller but growing, and the value proposition is exceptional."
